[COMMENTS]
STATION,Crump profile Flat V weir draining catchment containing coal measures and moorland and PWS reservoir. GENERAL: Crump profile Flat V weir in trapezoidal channel. Higher flows gauged from bridge upstream. Extreme flows bypass on right bank. Fairly low modular limit. Stream joins downstream, which causes drowning of gauging station weir. Pumped Eel pass installed 2015. STATION HYDROMETRY: Two ratings applied across period of record which are identical above 0.5m. The top section of the curve (out of bank) is derived using channel cross sections. Higher flows gauged from bridge upstream. Extreme flows bypass on right bank. FLOW RECORD: June 2007 peak flows estimated using flood curve. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2020 (WINFAP Files v9). FLOW REGIME: Contains Ogston PWS reservoir; substantial augmentation from mine pumping and sewage.
CATCHMENT,Upland catchment with moorland headwaters. Upper half of catchment drains Millstone Grit, partially blanketed with Boulder Clay. Bisects limestone and tuff inlier of Ashover. Lower half predominantly Coal Measures. Landuse predominantly moorland in the headwaters.
Qmed Suitability,Gauged to near QMED.
Pooling Suitability,Few high flow gaugings to validate out-of-bank rating curve limb.
[END]
